sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 native Swamp schedules, nothing installed on Nodes; DECISIONS Schedules (Nick 2026-11-02), R1.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: schedule:enable
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: schedule:enable 7f3c…<br/>Schedule UUID
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit schedule:enable 7f3c9a2e-41d0-4b8a-9c11-2f6e0d5b7a10`
  %%> - syntax: `<schedule> [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the UUID of the Schedule, as `schedule:list` shows it
  %%> When:
  %%> - after `schedule:create --no-start`, or for a copy that production preparation created disabled
  %%> Disable:
  %%> - there is no `schedule:disable` command or kind today
  %%> - disable is the same flow in reverse: the Gateway removes the trigger and records `disabled`, with no run and no Node work (R1)
  %%> - a fire that already started finishes, and its result is still recorded
  Note over GW: Validate the Schedule<br/>Schedule 7f3c… · Instance 42
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12, which runs Instance 42
  %%> - Schedule 7f3c… is active, not failed or removing
  %%> - Instance 42 is still on Node 12
  %%> Already enabled:
  %%> - the trigger is set again; enable is idempotent
  GW->>SW: Publish the trigger<br/>workflow.trigger.set
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - sets the native Swamp schedule trigger on serve (Node 209) for `task-command-run`
  %%> - there is no Node work, so no run starts (R1)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the calendar and the full intent recorded at create
  %%> - the command's vault key name, never the command
  alt Swamp confirms
    SW-->>GW: trigger set<br/>next fire 03:00
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the trigger is active, with its next fire time
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>desired state: enabled
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Schedule 7f3c… is recorded as enabled, only after Swamp confirms
    GW-->>CLI: Schedule enabled<br/>next fire 03:00
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the result at once; there is nothing to follow
  else Swamp refuses or is down
    SW--xGW: no confirmation<br/>refused or unreachable
    %%> When:
    %%> - serve on 209 does not answer, or refuses the trigger
    Note over GW: Keep the prior state<br/>desired state: disabled
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Schedule 7f3c… stays disabled; nothing changed
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; it is safe
    GW--xCLI: 503 publish unavailable<br/>swamp.schedule_publish_unavailable
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the error code; the Schedule is unchanged
  end
  loop each calendar fire
    Note over SW: Start a root run<br/>task-command-run
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - serve fires the trigger and starts one root run on 209
    %%> - the run has the Schedule's timeout as its time budget
    SW->>N: Run the command<br/>@swamp/ssh, as the Schedule's user
    %%> How:
    %%> - checks the user and the working directory on Node 12
    %%> - reads the command with `vault.get` and sends it on stdin
    %%> Runs as:
    %%> - the Schedule's user, in its working directory, with its shell
    N-->>SW: exit code, output
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the exit code; the output stays in the Swamp step
    SW-->>GW: Run finished<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the fire<br/>task #5141 · trigger: schedule
    %%> Result:
    %%> - each fire becomes a task, with trigger `schedule`
    %%> - `last_run_at` and `last_run_status` of Schedule 7f3c… are set
  end
